 ## Style prompt
 
 ```text
-Kannada bhavageethe-inspired lyrical ballad, warm intimate male voice, clear diction and expressive poetry-led phrasing. Quiet piano, lyrical violin, occasional bamboo flute and very light hand percussion. Relaxed four-beat flow with flexible space for long lines. Separate ಒಂದೊಂದಾಗಿ... ಒಂದೊಂದಾಗಿ... and pause fully after ನಾನೊಬ್ಬ ಕುಂಬಾರ. Held notes sustain beneath the breaths. Gentle stanza-to-stanza melodic variation, a quietly memorable refrain, an expanding mountain-and-moon bridge, then a soft lingering dream-weaving ending. Understated contemporary chamber sound. Shape melody around the Kannada poem's meaning; vary stanza endings subtly while keeping a recognisable refrain. Warm youthful delivery; calm, soulful joy, affection and wonder. Keep the pace unhurried throughout; finish with peaceful hope. No mournful delivery, driving beat or dramatic crescendo.
